Eviction: let Nova choose block migration

EvictionReconciler.liveMigrate in internal/controller/eviction/
controller.go builds servers.LiveMigrateOpts{BlockMigration: false}
and sends it at compute microversion 2.90. From microversion 2.25 on,
Nova requires both block_migration and host in os-migrateLive and
accepts a boolean or the string "auto" for block_migration
(nova/api/openstack/compute/schemas/migrate_server.py,
migrate_live_v2_25). With false, Nova refuses every server whose disks
live on the hypervisor's local storage with InvalidSharedStorage, so an
Eviction cannot move a server that boots from a local disk.

"auto" lets Nova decide per server: a block migration when source and
destination share no storage, a plain live migration when they do.
gophercloud v2.15.0 types LiveMigrateOpts.BlockMigration as *bool, so
the string needs an os-migrateLive body of its own. liveMigrateAuto is
that body, a servers.LiveMigrateOptsBuilder that sends "host": null
(Nova's scheduler picks the destination, as before) and
"block_migration": "auto". Leaving the field out is no alternative: the
2.25 schema rejects a body without it.

No upstream test pins the request body. The patch adds
TestLiveMigrateAutoBody, a plain Go test outside the Ginkgo suite, so
it runs without envtest; the CobaltCore image build runs it and fails
when it does not pass.

Applies-to: cobaltcore-dev/openstack-hypervisor-operator main @ a2baf3f4002e39ff93f105fae9594b357ba55b21

Upstream status: not submitted

